.TH ZVM-BUG 1 "August 2026" "ZVM" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zvm-bug \- start a ZVM bug report
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zvm bug
.RB [ --print ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open a prefilled issue form for the ZVM repository in a browser.
The form contains a report template and a collected description of the
environment ZVM is running in.
.PP
The report is not submitted by
.BR zvm .
Fill in what you did, what happened, and what you expected, review the
collected environment, and submit the issue yourself.
.PP
The collected environment includes the ZVM version, the target operating
system and architecture, the ZVM base directory, the values of the
.B ZVM_*
environment variables, the configured mirror list and version-map URLs, the
installed Zig versions, the selected Zig and ZLS versions, and the host kernel
and distribution.
.SH ANONYMIZATION
Paths inside the user's home directory are reported relative to
.BR ~ ,
so the report does not name the account it came from.
Paths outside the home directory are reported as they are.
.PP
Mirror-list and version-map URLs distributed with ZVM are reported verbatim.
A URL the user configured is replaced by a short digest, written as
.BR "custom sha256:" \fIdigest\fR .
.PP
The digest is a correlation tag rather than a secret.
A URL is drawn from a small enough set of candidates that hashing guesses
recovers it, so the digest serves only to distinguish one custom source from
another without publishing it.
Report contents should still be reviewed before submitting.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --print
Print the report URL instead of opening a browser.
Useful on machines with no browser, such as a remote shell or a container.
.SH BROWSER SELECTION
If
.B BROWSER
is set, it is run with the report URL as its argument.
Otherwise the platform handler is used:
.B open
on macOS,
.B "cmd /c start"
on Windows, and
.BR xdg-open ,
.BR www-browser ,
or
.B x-www-browser
elsewhere.
On other systems, a browser is only attempted when
.B DISPLAY
or
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
is set.
When no browser can be started, the URL is printed instead.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BROWSER
Command used to open the report URL.
.TP
.BR DISPLAY , " " WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Presence of either indicates a display server that can show a browser.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
zvm bug
zvm bug --print
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zvm (1),
.BR zvm-version (1),
.BR zvm-upgrade (1)
